[advisories] waived: GHSA-c83g-rgw3-j3cx (high, browserslist) — accepted until 2026-12-01: Unbounded memory growth in browserslist query caching. browserslist runs only while linting and bundling, over queries committed in this repository, and is absent from the production dependency tree, so no ConfoVHH user is exposed. The fix requires bumping the root lockfile, whose SHA-256 is bound into the frozen pre-label numbering contract at validation/hard-decoy-holdout-v3/vhh-sequence-contract-2026-08-29.json. That freeze exists so the analysis environment cannot move before the hard-decoy holdout is labelled and executed.
[advisories] waived: GHSA-73wf-gq98-2v4g (high, browserslist) — accepted until 2026-12-01: Crash and prototype write when browserslist parses an untrusted browserslist-stats.json. This repository ships no browserslist-stats.json and never parses one from an external source. As above, browserslist is build-time only and absent from the production dependency tree.
[advisories] waived: GHSA-px8p-9vwx-vf98 (moderate, fflate) — accepted until 2026-12-01: fflate unzipSync can enter an infinite loop on a malformed ZIP64 archive. ConfoVHH never reaches that code. fflate is pulled in only by vinext's Open Graph image generation, through satori's font parser; vinext is a devDependency that serves the local dev server, the shipped artifact is the static SPA built by vite build --config vite.vercel.config.ts, and `npm ls fflate --omit=dev` is empty. No ConfoVHH source file references fflate or unzipSync, and the product accepts coordinate and PAE files rather than archives, so there is no path by which a user-supplied ZIP reaches this parser. The fix requires bumping the root lockfile, whose SHA-256 (0dc4d6b441b0faf3c4ab3783115469cfc720fb8fc7cae36d225bc001ba174f54) is bound into the frozen pre-label numbering contract at validation/hard-decoy-holdout-v3/vhh-sequence-contract-2026-08-29.json. That freeze exists so the analysis environment cannot move before the hard-decoy holdout is labelled and executed.
[advisories] pass: no unreviewed advisory at or above moderate; production tree clean; 3 reviewed exception(s).
